###  https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-recyclability#TextileWaste
:TextileWaste rdf:type owl:Class ;
              rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-core#TextileProduct> ;
              <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://susproc.jrc.ec.europa.eu/product-bureau/sites/default/files/2025-12/Textile-Prep-Study_3rd-Milestone_20251212.pdf> ;
              rdfs:comment "Textile product that the holder discards, intends to discard or is required to discard."@en ;
              rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-recyclability> ;
              rdfs:label "Textile waste"@en ;
              <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-connector#modellingNote> "TextileWaste represents a textile product in a waste status. The generation-stage category is supplied separately through hasWasteSourceType."@en ;
              <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-connector#sourceLocator> "JRC Preparatory Study, relevant section, printed page 15, lines 188-212; JRC Preparatory Study, Section 9.2.4, printed page 130, lines 3487-3509."@en ;
              <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-connector#sourceType> <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-connector#adaptedDefinition> .


###  https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-recyclability#TextileWasteSourceConcept
